 prompt for a single-line commit message, and commits with the generated message. It includes a spinner animation for visual feedback during generation and allows manual message override when needed. The solution transforms generic \"wip\" commits into descriptive messages that help teammates understand code changes.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/fb11f758c1e457980f187d6eecb8c991?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-26T08:56:32.000Z"},{"id":"Qke8krf05","title":"Running PHP 8.5 with Laravel Octane and FrankenPHP: The Missing Manual (Fix the 8.4 binary trap)","url":"https://freek.dev/2976-running-php-85-with-laravel-octane-and-frankenphp-the-missing-manual-fix-the-84-binary-trap","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/running-php-8-5-with-laravel-octane-and-frankenphp-the-missing-manual-fix-the-8-4-binary-trap--qke8krf05","summary":"The default FrankenPHP binary installed via Laravel Octane's artisan command is statically compiled with PHP 8.4, preventing use of PHP 8.5 features or custom system extensions. This guide provides a solution for developers who need to run PHP 8.5 with Laravel Octane and FrankenPHP by working around this version lock.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/84acfc9a3e54d0dd85271d4954ac475f?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":26,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-21T13:37:47.000Z"},{"id":"WxxatAu48","title":"From dd() to Ray: A Debugging Workflow That Doesn't Break Your Flow","url":"https://freek.dev/2974-from-dd-to-ray-a-debugging-workflow-that-doesnt-break-your-flow","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/from-dd-to-ray-a-debugging-workflow-that-doesn-t-break-your-flow-wxxatau48","summary":"The article appears to discuss debugging workflows in PHP development, specifically comparing the dd() function (dump and die) to Ray, a debugging tool. The content suggests a workflow approach that maintains developer productivity without interrupting the development flow.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/64a64d50ea5cacb36d29e30a75e7b4f6?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-19T13:07:11.000Z"},{"id":"loLeQ7V5s","title":"Livewire 4 Deep Dive: Components, Performance & New Directives","url":"https://freek.dev/2973-livewire-4-deep-dive-components-performance-new-directives","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/livewire-4-deep-dive-components-performance-new-directives-loleq7v5s","summary":"Livewire 4 brings new features for Laravel development, including enhanced components, performance improvements, and new directives. The release aims to streamline building interactive Laravel applications with its latest capabilities.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9cfff5dcad27ea9acde47e37570837d2?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-16T13:49:36.000Z"},{"id":"hqperYcLe","title":"Why I made my portfolio feel like a terminal","url":"https://freek.dev/2972-behind-the-terminal","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/behind-the-terminal-hqperycle","summary":"A portfolio website was designed with a terminal-inspired interface. The article explains the motivation behind choosing a terminal aesthetic and the technical implementation details of creating this retro command-line look and feel for a web-based portfolio.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a7457b4e2ad3706c82fde28cf2eedef9?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":71,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2026-01-15T13:57:36.000Z"},{"id":"ya2qiAh3Y","title":"The hidden costs of frictionless development","url":"https://freek.dev/2971-what-gets-lost-when-everything-is-effortless","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-gets-lost-when-everything-is-effortless--ya2qiah3y","summary":"Explores the trade-offs of removing friction from development workflows and tools. Questions whether making everything effortless comes at the cost of deeper understanding, intentionality, or valuable learning experiences. Examines the balance between convenience and the benefits that some friction can provide.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f3ef4332806a55415d413d135b3b0df0?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-14T13:01:53.000Z"},{"id":"AAHPstPxp","title":"Tech AI layoffs discussion","url":"https://freek.dev/2970-the-truth-behind-tech-ai-layoffs","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-truth-behind-tech-ai-layoffs-aahpstpxp","summary":"This appears to be a video link about AI-related layoffs in the tech industry. The actual content shown consists primarily of promotional material for a hosting platform (Sevalla) and newsletter signup information, without substantive discussion of the layoff topic promised in the title.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/cdd78da6728e453fd7530b46965f7520?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-13T13:01:25.000Z"},{"id":"uTnJ1hOO4","title":"Symfony 20 year!","url":"https://freek.dev/2969-symfony-20-year","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/symfony-20-year--utnj1hoo4","summary":"Symfony celebrates its 20th anniversary this year. The article promises to explore statistics and highlights from two decades of the PHP framework's impact on web development history.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/12127e1f46eeb1c5f3d4711b6f704df1?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-12T13:36:32.000Z"},{"id":"3sg5edEwt","title":"Eval Testing LLMs in PHPUnit","url":"https://freek.dev/2966-eval-testing-llms-in-phpunit","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/eval-testing-llms-in-phpunit-3sg5edewt","summary":"LLM prompts can fail silently without obvious errors. This guide demonstrates how to implement evaluation testing for LLM outputs